🏗️ Project Overview

The Enterprise Learning Management System (ELMS) is designed with microservices architecture to support large-scale training operations, multi-department learning structures, role-based access management, and advanced reporting.

The system enables global enterprise learning through modular services that scale independently.

🔧 Microservices Architecture

This LMS application is composed of multiple independently deployable services:

🧩 Core Services
Service	Description	Database
Auth Service	User authentication, JWT, RBAC	PostgreSQL
User/Profile Service	Learners, instructors, roles, departments	PostgreSQL
Course Service	Courses, modules, lessons, materials	MySQL
Enrollment Service	Course enrollment, tracking, progress	MySQL
Assessment Service	Quizzes, exams, grading	PostgreSQL
Certificate Service	Completion certificates & validations	MySQL
Notification Service	Email, SMS, in-app alerts	PostgreSQL
Reporting Service	Analytics, dashboards, activity logs	PostgreSQL
Gateway/API Aggregator	Routing, load balancing	—
Discovery Service (Eureka)	Service registration & discovery	—
Config Server	Centralized configuration	—
🌟 Key Enterprise LMS Features
Status	Feature
🟩 JWT-Based Authentication + RBAC with Spring Security
🟩 Course Management (Modules, Lessons, Resources)
🟩 Employee Learning Path Assignments
🟩 Progress Tracking & Completion Metrics
🟩 Quiz & Assessment Engine
🟩 Certificate Generation & Validation
🟩 Multi-Tenant Support (optional)
🟩 Service-to-Service Authentication
🟩 Centralized Logging & Monitoring
🟩 Distributed Config, Gateway & Discovery Services

🟩 All modules follow microservices best practices and are independently deployable.

⚙️ Technology Stack
Layer	Technology
Backend Framework	Spring Boot / Spring Cloud
Databases	MySQL + PostgreSQL (per service specialization)
Service Discovery	Eureka Server
API Gateway	Spring Cloud Gateway
Configuration	Spring Cloud Config
Security	Spring Security + JWT
Build Tool	Maven
Containerization	Docker / Docker Compose
Messaging/Eventing	Kafka / RabbitMQ (optional module)
Documentation	Swagger / OpenAPI
Testing	JUnit • Mockito
📘 API Gateway Endpoint Overview
Category	Description	Example Gateway Route
Auth Service	Login, refresh tokens	/api/auth/login
Users	Manage learner & instructor profiles	/api/users/{id}
Courses	CRUD operations for courses	/api/courses
Enrollments	Enroll learners & track activity	/api/enrollments
Assessments	Quiz creation, submissions, scoring	/api/assessments
Certificates	Issue and validate certificates	/api/certificates/{id}
Notifications	Alerts & reminders	/api/notifications/send
Reports	Learning analytics & dashboards	/api/reports/overview
🐳 Running the System with Docker
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/asohyannick/enterprise-lms-microservices
cd enterprise-lms-microservices

# Build and start all services
docker-compose up --build


Each service includes its own Dockerfile and automatically connects to the right database container.

